/// Negative example: `const` initialised by a fn call rather
/// than a constant expression. The diagnostics test harness
/// asserts the type checker rejects this.
///
/// expect-error: const` requires a compile-time constant expression
/// Test fixture used as the non-constant initializer.
fn get_time() -> int { 42 }
/// Test fixture: violates the const-only-constants rule.
fn main() {
    const now = get_time()
    println(string(now))
}
